"reference":"knowledge-record:b5cd9836e2504bc24927d0d649fa655c76ca2e5a249db7c5fb1f764c3fdf1592","status":"provisional","type":"shared-note"},"text":"# Keep documentation snippet extensions and explicit lint scope together\n\nFor the checked annotation includes, review preferred proper .js/.json file extensions so editor tooling could help authors, rather than renamed _js files to avoid lint. The patch adds explicit includes-directory exceptions to eslint-ignores.config.mjs and tools/lint/license.yml and a separate license file. The reviewer questioned treating these manual examples as generic generated or third-party code. Codespell remained a follow-up idea, with a warning that stored API property names cannot simply be renamed. This is scoped historical snippet practice, not permission to disable production lint or a legal-clearance conclusion.\n\nScope: Extension documentation snippet tooling.\n\n## Evidence\n\n[Lesson record](../records/b5cd9836e2504bc24927d0d649fa655c76ca2e5a249db7c5fb1f764c3fdf1592.json).\n\n- [Supporting record](../records/3046d1132d7726354b99bfc9dccf0dde5b1ff3fee2352b0596e8843efd8c66f8.json)\n- [Supporting record](../records/85c88f786a3aedc6e97a2123d2c55ed0298f82ea230debff5f3c04de7f91526c.json)\n\n## Validation and limits\n\nStatus: **provisional**. Quoted evidence supports the claim; its interpretation still needs current-source checks.","title":"Keep documentation snippet extensions and explicit lint scope together","version":1,"visibility":"shared"}
